        "tipo": "gramatica",
        "min": 6,
        "titulo": "Gender in one minute",
        "explicacao": "Every Russian noun has a gender, and the adjective agrees with it. Masculine: ends in a consonant (дом, стол). Feminine: ends in -а or -я (книга, машина). Neuter: ends in -о or -е (окно). The adjective changes with it: новый (m), новая (f), новое (n). Careful: gender belongs to the Russian word, not to the thing: книга (book) is feminine, while окно (window) is neuter. English has nothing like this, so learn each noun together with its ending. You will practise this calmly in lesson 11.",
